\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Derived the exact consequence of the Q derivative rate and counterchecked two unjustified asymptotic/global-attraction inferences.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the supplied definition, catalogue wording, source qualifications and reference entries for 30003921. The historical source/context and inherited status are retained; no fresh literature or novelty certification is claimed. No external theorem is used without proof in this attempt; explicit model assumptions are distinguished from facts about the source model.

\paragraph{What the stated rates would imply.} Suppose only that \(|Q_\tau|\le Ce^{-3\tau/2}\) for \(\tau\ge\tau_0\). Integrating from \(\tau\) to \(T\) makes \(Q(T)\) Cauchy and proves an actual limit with
\[
 |Q(\tau)-Q_\infty|\le\frac{2C}{3}e^{-3\tau/2}.
\]
In contrast, \(V_\tau\to1/2\) does not imply convergence of \(V-\tau/2\). The explicit function \(V(\tau)=\tau/2+\log\tau\), \(\tau\ge1\), has the required derivative limit but an unbounded offset. Absolute integrability of the derivative error is a sufficient extra hypothesis guaranteeing that stronger conclusion; conditionally convergent errors may also suffice.
\paragraph{Testing local-to-global attraction.} Even smooth scalar dynamics may have a local attractor but fail globally: \(\dot x=-x+x^3\) points toward zero for \(|x|<1\), whereas for \(x\ge\sqrt2\), \(\dot x\ge x^3/2\). Integrating \((x^{-2})'=-2\dot x/x^3\le-1\) proves finite-time blowup for such initial data. This is a diagnostic ODE, not an Einstein solution; it shows why local stability cannot replace an absorbing-region estimate.
\paragraph{Source comparison.} For the source system, the conserved \(B\), constraints and non-Gowdy exclusions must supply that missing global control. Neither the global \(B_0\) attractor, the non-\(B_0\) local attractor with both rates, nor its globality is proved. The first gap is a coercive estimate forcing every admissible orbit into the proven local regime, with constants compatible with \(B\). The displayed consequences do not change the inherited status.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked the exponential integral, the logarithmic V offset and explicit finite-time ODE growth; did not identify the diagnostic ODE with a spacetime. This is a GPT-6 Astra Ultra self-audit, not independent human verification. Prompt A drafting followed by prompt B scope/dependency/boundary self-audit. Checked the exponential integral, the logarithmic V offset and explicit finite-time ODE growth; did not identify the diagnostic ODE with a spacetime. The remaining gap is: Establish a coercive absorbing estimate for the actual constrained T2 equations, then control the nonzero-B attractor and rates. Unresolved status and zero original-target completion are retained.

Coordinator checked the exponential tail integration, divergent-offset example and finite-time ODE comparison. Absolute integrability is correctly described as sufficient rather than necessary. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

